  "chainid_opcode_across_upgrades": {
    "_info": {
      "comment": "CHAINID stores the chain identifier at slot zero. Two assertions in one body: the opcode does not exist before Phoenix, so the upgrades below it write no storage at all; and from Phoenix onward it returns this chain's identifier, which is not Ethereum's. Filled at Ethereum's equivalent upgrade the same body returns 1, so no upstream fixture can stand in for this one even though the rule sets are otherwise identical.",
      "oracle": "core-geth production, evm t8n at each upgrade's rules, chain id 61",
      "oracle-version": "v1.12.21-unstable",
      "generated": "2026-08-21",
      "signing": "txbytes carries the signed transaction; the signing key is a filling input, not a fixture field, and the harness reads `sender`.",
      "unfilled-no-fork-name": "No expectation for ETC_DieHard, ETC_Gotham, ETC_DefuseDifficultyBomb, ETC_Thanos: the generator's fork table has no name for them, so their rules cannot be selected. A tooling gap, not a claim that the case does not apply.",
      "unfilled-not-a-state-rule": "No expectation for ETC_DAOFork, ETC_DAOWars, ETC_FrontierThawing, ETC_MESSOff, ETC_MESSOn: these change no state-transition rule, so a state fixture has nothing to assert about them. Covering them needs block-level or chain-selection tests."
